.TH HYPRWINDOWS 1 "November 2026" "hyprwindows" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hyprwindows \- Hyprland window rules manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hyprwindows
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hyprwindows
is a Qt 6 window for viewing and editing Hyprland
.B hl.window_rule()
calls. It can compare those rules with the windows
.B hyprctl
currently reports, and it can suggest rules for installed apps listed in an appmap.
.PP
There is no command-line editing mode. The window has five pages: Rules, Windows, Review, Pipeline, and Actions.
.PP
Saving updates a
.I rules = { }
table in place, writing default rules, then tag rules, then overrides. A file with no such table is rewritten only when it contains window-rule calls, blanks, and comments. A mixed
.I hyprland.lua
is left untouched.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show usage information.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save. A
.I rules = { }
table is updated in place. A mixed
.I hyprland.lua
is left untouched.
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
New rule.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y
Undo / redo.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Reload rules from disk.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Filter the rule list.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua
Scanned for a
.B require()
that points at the window rules module. A dedicated
.I rules.lua
is preferred over editing the main config.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/hyprwindows/appmap.json
Installed app-to-window-class map. A
.I data/appmap.json
in the working directory is preferred when it exists.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hyprctl (1),
.BR hyprland (1)
.SH AUTHOR
hyprwindows contributors
